This assumes encode returns an unpadded, one-dimensional ID list and supports these arguments. Adapt other libraries explicitly and check for implicit truncation. Batch processing can improve throughput, but exclude padding with attention_mask. Also report skipped zero-word records and reasons; emoji-only or punctuation-only records can retain separate token accounting rather than disappearing from usage estimates.

Verify counts and weighting with hand-checkable fixtures, then test empty strings, mixed-language text, combining characters, rare scripts, and long documents. Save tokenizer versions, corpus hashes, normalization policies, and reference-segmenter versions. Retain document-level observations for percentiles and document-bootstrap uncertainty; resample parallel examples together to preserve pairing.

